<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Controller (VFEP v4.03,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are the
    Controller's, its spider mine module left off. Plating, tags, the market-value references
    and the UltraMechtech gate follow the armor's header, as does the art note.

    Tuning: the pads are the set's command piece, the one a mechanitor's vanilla utility gear
    has no single answer to.
    - MechControlGroups 1, Biotech's control pack (Steel 100, ComponentIndustrial 6).
    - HackingSpeed 0.2, a fifth faster at the hacking the overlord trait leaves the pilot
      (Research). No vanilla apparel carries it; it is the pads' processors turned on a
      terminal, and it keeps the set's bandwidth on the helmet and the armor.
    - No MechBandwidth: the helmet's 12 and the armor's 8 are the set's 20.
    - costList ComponentSpacer 2 / Plasteel 60 / SignalChip 2. The first two are the
      Controller shoulders' price, the plasteel the 10th-gen shoulder-to-armor ratio, roughly
      0.4 (Siegebreaker 60/145, Guardian 80/200, Controller 60/150, Sarcophagus 60/145, Brute
      60/160), of the armor's 150. The chips are the diabolus's drop at the price of Biotech's
      bandwidth pack (SignalChip 2), the command gear a mechanitor straps on outside a
      warcasket, so the command range has a price and the set's chips climb from the
      diabolus's here through the war queen's on the helmet to the apocriton's on the armor.

    Command range (the CommandRangeExtension entry, Source/1.6/CommandRange/): a mechanitor
    wearing the pads may order their drafted mechs anywhere on the map they share (scope
    CurrentMap), where vanilla stops every move and attack order at 24.9 cells from the overseer.
    The pads carry it as the set's command relays, leaving the helmet the bandwidth; the mod
    settings may move the entry to the helmet, widen it to every mechanitor or switch it off,
    and override the scope (Anywhere drops the same-map rule too; Radius keeps vanilla's shape
    at the radius below) and the radius, which is the Radius scope's reach and the settings
    slider's default, left at vanilla's 24.9 so switching to that scope starts from vanilla.
    normalRadius, unset here and so vanilla's too, is the range without the set as the settings
    window quotes it; a mod that moves the range for everyone has both written by its compat
    root (Combat Extended's 43.9, 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/CommandRange.xml).
    The settings write every choice back onto this entry at startup and when the window closes;
    CommandRange's header has the vanilla call paths and the rules.

    ApparelExtension priority 1, for the reason in the armor def's header: the
    VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase parent carries its own, and only the highest-priority copy
    keeps its fields whole (Merge still ORs the parent's isUnifiedApparel in). Any new
    ApparelExtension field for this piece goes on this entry.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml and the VGE vacuum patch leave shoulder pads alone, as VFEP's and
    VGE1's own patches do for VFEP's. The 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root rescales the
    plating and adds bulk, as CE's does for VFEP's.

    Draw order: a worn apparel node's altitude is its drawData offset y (added verbatim by
    PawnRenderTree.TryGetMatrix) plus PawnRenderUtility.AltitudeForLayer(layer), 0.000366 per
    layer unit, the layer being the parent's base (ApparelBody 20, ApparelHead 70) plus the
    piece's index among that parent's apparel; the y offsets on VFEP's bases are what order the
    pieces. Only this piece moves, so every helmet and armor, ours or VFEP's, keeps its VFEP
    altitude and foundry mix-and-match stays consistent.
    - South 0.014 (base 0.02, which lands at 0.027 to 0.028, just over the helmets' 0.027):
      the art wants the helmet over the pauldron edges, so 0.021 to 0.022, at least 0.004 under
      any helmet and 0.003 over the shell (0.017 to 0.018), above post-apparel wounds (layer
      30, 0.011) and firefoam (40, 0.015). Hair and beard (about 0.022) can draw over them on a
      bare head, as hair does over shoulders anyway.
    North, east and west inherit the base's 0.2, 0.02 and 0.02: XmlInheritance merges
    same-named elements recursively, so only the changed facing is listed.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>OLWC_WarcasketShoulders_Overlord</defName>
    <label>overlord warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with standard protection, equipped with command relays that let the pilot order mechs anywhere on the map.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with standard protection, equipped with command relays that let the pilot order mechs anywhere on the map.\n\nA 10th-generation design from the government program that rebuilt captured pirate rigs around its own power armor and gave them to veterans who could no longer serve any other way. The Overlord was its rig for veteran mechanitors, who would command their own mechs in the field rather than join a squad.\n\nThe Overlord series is meant for a mechanitor who goes into battle alone, with only their mechs beside them. The core in the shell holds only a few charges and regains them slowly, so they are best saved for the mechs that matter most. When a fight cannot wait, it can be reloaded with advanced components. The helmet greatly increases the pilot's bandwidth at some cost to their aim, the shoulders carry command relays that reach mechs anywhere on the map, and the arms are left free for smithing and hacking. Because the plating is far tougher than a mechanitor's usual armor, the pilot can lead from the front line rather than from behind the mechs.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordShoulders</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>22</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>22</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MechControlGroups>1</MechControlGroups>
      <HackingSpeed>0.2</HackingSpeed>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.1</VacuumResistance>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentSpacer>2</ComponentSpacer>
      <Plasteel>60</Plasteel>
      <SignalChip>2</SignalChip>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
      <li>UltraMechtech</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketOverlord/WarcasketOverlordShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <!-- Under the helmet facing south; see "Draw order" in the header. -->
      <drawData>
        <dataSouth><offset>(0, 0.014, 0)</offset></dataSouth>
      </drawData>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
      </li>
      <li Class="OverlordWarcasket.CommandRangeExtension">
        <scope>CurrentMap</scope>
        <radius>24.9</radius>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
